    <!-- FAQ Items -->
    <string name="faq_q1">What does LinkScrub do?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">LinkScrub cleans web addresses (URLs) by stripping tracking parameters (such as utm_*, fbclid, gclid, and session markers). It also unshortens short links (bit.ly, t.co) so you can see where they really lead before sharing or visiting.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Does LinkScrub store or upload my links?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">No. LinkScrub is 100% on-device and privacy-first. Your links, parameters, and browsing history are never transmitted to external cloud servers. All link analysis and history are kept strictly on your phone.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Will scrubbing break important features like YouTube video timestamps?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">No. LinkScrub features domain-aware intelligence that preserves essential parameters (such as \'t=…\' start timestamps on YouTube videos and core product paths on Amazon) while stripping tracking garbage (like \'si=\' or referral tags).</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">How do I use LinkScrub from other apps?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Whenever you want to clean a link in Twitter, WhatsApp, Chrome, or Reddit, tap \'Share\' in that app and choose \'LinkScrub\'. LinkScrub will automatically receive, scrub, and allow you to copy or re-share the clean URL immediately.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">What is Quick-Clean Mode?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">Quick-Clean Mode allows you to paste a link and have it immediately sanitized and copied to your clipboard with a single tap, bypassing intermediate review steps for speedy sharing.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">How does unshortening work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">Short URLs (e.g. bit.ly, t.co) redirect through one or more hops to their destination. LinkScrub follows these HTTP redirect headers on-device with built-in cyclic loop detection to reveal the genuine destination safely.</string>

    <!-- How It Works Items -->
    <string name="how_it_works_step1_number">1</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step1_title">Input &amp; Detection</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step1_desc">Paste a URL, scan a QR code, or share directly to LinkScrub from another app. LinkScrub automatically parses links even when embedded in conversational text blocks.</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step2_number">2</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step2_title">Inspect &amp; Parameter Stripping</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step2_desc">LinkScrub inspects query tokens and categorizes them into known tracking markers (UTM, Facebook fbclid, Google Ads gclid, TikTok telemetry) and legitimate parameters. You can toggle any parameter on or off.</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step3_number">3</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step3_title">Unshortening &amp; Open Graph Preview</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_step3_desc">If the URL is a shortlink, redirect headers are resolved with cyclic loop protection. Rich metadata (title, preview image, description) is fetched so you can verify the target safely before sharing.</string>

